.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt NQSETTMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqsettmp ,
.Nm nqdsettmp
.Nd learn of the temporary files the library writes through
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.In nqd.h
.Vt typedef void (*nqtmpfn)(int ev, const char *path, void *user);
.Ft int
.Fn nqsettmp "nqtmpfn fn" "void *user"
.Ft int
.Fn nqdsettmp "nqtmpfn fn" "void *user"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The capsule layer writes each file of a seal
.Po
.Xr nqseal 3 ,
.Fn nqseal2 ,
.Xr nqtsput 3 ,
.Xr nqersput 3
.Pc
to a new temporary file beside it, made with
.Dv O_EXCL ,
and renames it into place once it is whole; the data layer does the
same for the data record and the files it writes
.Pq Xr nqdsave 3 , Xr nqdsyn 3 .
A temporary name that is taken is never written: the next of up to 16
names is tried.
.Fn nqsettmp
and
.Fn nqdsettmp
set a function each layer calls about these files, so that a caller
that is stopped by a signal can remove the one being written, and never
a file that only has the same name:
.Fa fn
is called from the thread doing the work with the event
.Fa ev ,
the file's path (the folder as given, a slash, and the name) and
.Fa user .
The events:
.Bl -tag -width NQTNEW
.It Dv NQTPRE
Right before an attempt to make
.Fa path .
.It Dv NQTNEW
The attempt made it: the file is the library's.
.It Dv NQTNOT
The attempt did not (the name was taken, or another error): the file of
that name, if any, is not the library's.
.It Dv NQTEND
The file was renamed into place, or removed.
.El
.Pp
.Dv NQTPRE
is always followed by
.Dv NQTNEW
or
.Dv NQTNOT
for the same path, with nothing done in between, so a caller that holds
its signals from
.Dv NQTPRE
until the next event never misses the file nor takes another one for
it.
.Xr noqtis 1
does that.
The function must not call back into the library.
The settings are global, and may be changed at any time, also while
other threads call into the library, as
.Xr nqsetprog 3 .
A
.Dv NULL
.Fa fn
stops the calls.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Both return
.Dv NQOK .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static void note(int ev, const char *path, void *u) {
  (void)u;
  fprintf(stderr, "%s %s\en", ev == NQTPRE ? "try" : ev == NQTNEW ? "made"
          : ev == NQTNOT ? "not made" : "done", path);
}
\&...
nqsettmp(note, NULL);
nqdsettmp(note, NULL);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqdnew 3 ,
.Xr nqseal 3 ,
.Xr nqsetprog 3
